 "Use Prompts from the ",
 ButtonBox["Prompt Repository",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://resources.wolframcloud.com/PromptRepository/"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://resources.wolframcloud.com/PromptRepository/"]
}], "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"2b2c9bed-6006-4e2c-b2d3-6f2e33628c6a"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"LLMSynthesize", "[", 
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"LLMPrompt", "[", "\"\<WilliamPlaywright\>\"", "]"}], 
    ",", "\"\<How to use the Wolfram Language function TextSummarize?\>\""}], 
   "}"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[11]:=",ExpressionUUID->"f2d2dd3b-0708-4a0d-a95f-577de3ae8921"],

Cell[BoxData["\<\"O Wolfram Language, through its coded vein,\\nA function \
named TextSummarize dost reign.\\nGive it a text, lengthy and verbose,\\nAnd \
henceforth it will create no ghosts.\\nFor in its heart, it seeks to \
know,\\nThe essence of the tale below,\\nReducing all into a span,\\nThat can \
be grasped by common man.\\n\\nFirst, thou must approach thy line of \
code,\\nAnd onto 't place thy heavy load:\\nAn input text dost thou \
supply,\\nAnd watch as it begins to fly.\\nWithin one line it doth \
condense,\\nTransforming all into sense.\\n\\nSo, pray use it well, and with \
respect,\\nFor its power is vast if correctly kept.\\n\\\"TextSummarize[text]\
\\\" is what you pen,\\nAnd lo! You've got the gist again!\"\>"], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[11]=",ExpressionUUID->"18bc4932-6291-4406-8e92-5f76e6727771"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"LLMSynthesize", "[", 
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"LLMPrompt", "[", "\"\<ELI5\>\"", "]"}], 
    ",", "\"\<How to use the Wolfram Language function TextSummarize?\>\""}], 
   "}"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[12]:=",ExpressionUUID->"bef448dc-b36a-4bac-a705-b96962953a19"],

Cell[BoxData["\<\"The TextSummarize function is a clever tool your computer \
can use to take a really long piece of writing and make it shorter. Imagine \
if you had to read a whole book, but you wanted to know what it was about in \
just a few sentences. That's what TextSummarize does!\\n\\nTo use it, we tell \
the computer we want to use TextSummarize by typing TextSummarize[\\\"\\\"], \
and we put the long piece of writing we want shortened inside the quotes. But \
it's not a toy and should only be used with the help of adults, as we need to \
be careful to use it properly!\"\>"], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[12]=",ExpressionUUID->"10e154ed-2210-4363-9cff-f84c73a3414f"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

